On Thu, Apr 08, 2004 at 05:28:58PM -0700, Robin Lee Powell wrote:
> I am considering an extension to allow 'si' or 'sa' at the beginning of
> text (presumably to erase stuff from the proceeding utterance).  The
> morphology needs massive amounts of work, and ideally I'd like to get
> Nora and Pierre's full algorithm encoded. 

Do you mean the algorithm for breaking a speech stream into words, or the 
algorithm for telling whether the words are valid? The former is done, except 
for the option that always requires a pause before a cmevla and being tested 
by someone else; but the latter I'm not finished encoding myself.

I am working, when I can find time for it, on the complete brivla validity 
test. I think I got the tosmabru test working right, but it is claiming that 
{lekybumlatu} and {stanybrulspa} are valid. (The former is {le kybu mlatu} 
run together; {brulspa} is the slinku'i of {tebrulspa}, a plant of the mint 
family.)

